  "content": {
    "id": "p28-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Bag A has three red and five green balls. Bag B has four red and two green balls. A ball is drawn from A; if red, it is placed in B, otherwise it is discarded. Then a ball is drawn from B. Find the probability that the two balls drawn have different colours.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{11}{21}$",
      "worked": "Different colours occur along the red–green or green–red paths. After a red draw from A, B contains five red and two green balls. After a green draw from A, B is unchanged.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{different colours})&=\\frac38\\times\\frac27+\\frac58\\times\\frac46\\\\P(\\text{different colours})&=\\frac{3}{28}+\\frac{5}{12}\\\\P(\\text{different colours})&=\\frac{9+35}{84}\\\\P(\\text{different colours})&=\\frac{11}{21}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 36
  },
